For thirty years, Dubai sold access to the Middle East without exposure to it. Iran sits across the water. Iraq is nearby. Yemen’s war is within range. The region hasn’t been stable in living memory and is unlikely ', 'closing_passage': 's. Now Dubai. The pattern isn’t coincidental. The world that made neutral spaces possible — unipolar, relatively stable, with shared assumptions about what was off-limits — is ending. What replaces it doesn’t have the same rules.

The buildings will be repaired. The foundations are another question.', 'native_item_note': None, 'continuation_evidence': None, 'page_column_locator': None, 'correction_sidecar_reference': None, 'review_basis': 'Selected source-native DOM/body opening-ending structure inspected; no full old-corpus body rescan'}

