{'native_body_boundary': '#article-body', 'selected_raw_reference': 'work_packages/M1_source_access/24_newspaper_coverage_successor_20261006/worker/raw/6a88ff4ce1016c9e34edef35.bin', 'raw_sha256_reused': 'e3254da58d16bc7a07756ee74b47586a8cb4df08cc2810d48923cce47b38ce6c', 'body_selector_matches_observed': 1, 'native_headings_observed': [], 'opening_passage': 'Lin Miaoke, a nine-year-old Chinese girl who performed at the opening ceremony of the Beijing Olympics returns to the Xizhongjie Primary School of Dongcheng District in Beijing. A 7-year-old Chinese girl's face was "not suitable" for the Ol', 'closing_passage': 'd she was in an Olympics ad earlier this year, China Daily reported.

Her father, Lin Hui, told China Daily he learned Miaoke would be "singing" only 15 minutes before the opening ceremony began.

Lin "still cannot believe his daughter has become an international singing sensation," the report said.', 'native_item_note': None, 'continuation_evidence': None, 'page_column_locator': None, 'correction_sidecar_reference': None, 'review_basis': 'Selected source-native DOM/body opening-ending structure inspected; no full old-corpus body rescan'}

