{'native_body_boundary': 'main.container > article.article', 'selected_raw_reference': 'work_packages/M1_source_access/24_newspaper_coverage_successor_20261006/worker/raw/b54294ea2aef5627993050dd.bin', 'raw_sha256_reused': '3ae18a9996b1a7e4ad01f975d105cdcacda48a33d1e1bd6cfec5b773ffa28fde', 'body_selector_matches_observed': 1, 'native_headings_observed': [{'tag': 'h1', 'text': 'MIT Police Accused Of Using ‘Excessive Force’ in 2006 Arrest'}, {'tag': 'h2', 'text': ''}, {'tag': 'h4', 'text': 'By Nick Semenkovich Sep. 19, 2008'}], 'opening_passage': 'A Waltham, Mass. resident is suing the MIT Police for “excessive force” and violations of his constitutional rights during his Feb. 2006 arrest.

